  "body": "What is wrong: the test `multi_pass_contour_simulates_with_meridian_parity` in the `lathe_field_sim` test binary takes about 107 s in debug. The rule is to move a test over about 60 s to the heavy lane or to use a smaller fixture.\n\nEvidence: PR #1838 comment on #1715. The test is one field-engine job, so a split gives no gain.\n\nPart of #1715.\n\nDone means: the test uses a smaller fixture and runs in under 60 s in debug. Or it is `#[ignore]`d with a reason that names the heavy lane, and the release tier lists it. Its asserts stay the same.\n",
